  "task": {
    "objective": "Each trader delivers two goods of its private required type to its own dock. Exactly two physical goods of each type exist.",
    "natural_termination": "All three traders have delivered two goods; otherwise truncate at tick 160. A finished trader is inactive and accepts only wait.",
    "interaction": "One-slot inventory, narrow routes, public reservations and escrow commitments constrain others. Offers bind existing carried goods at loading bays. Reciprocal offers atomically swap a pair; if no pair clears, a compatible three-way cycle can clear atomically. No goods are copied or created.",
    "observation_access": "Each role sees all public yard, physical goods, reservations, posted offers and deliberately broadcast truthful signals, plus only its own private demand one-hot. Private order entities have identity-matrix visibility. A reveal action or an observed delivery may legitimately disclose demand; hidden order fields never enter another row or public scene attribute.",
    "transition_order": "Movement uses old occupancy, reservation and escrow state; timers decay; inventory and deliveries settle in rotating order; reservations, offers and truthful signals update; rotating bilateral matching has priority over three-way cycle clearing; expiring/settled offers clear, then joint terminal state is evaluated."
  },
  "invariant_notes": [
    "Every good retains its identity and type; owner is ground -1, a single trader 0..2 or delivered 3. Two goods of each type remain in the full state.",
    "No trader carries more than one good; each active offer names that traders actual escrowed good.",
    "Bilateral settlement swaps both owners together. Three-way settlement permutes all three owners; there is no credit or duplication.",
    "Reservation owner and ttl agree; offer ttl lies in [0,4], reservation ttl in [0,6], signal ttl in [0,5].",
    "All active trader positions are distinct walkable cells. Orders and offers may visually share a cell with their actual dock or carrier.",
    "Private demand is a random permutation of the three types. Knowing one type constrains the other two; inference from the public distribution or deliberate signals is legitimate.",
    "No demand-dependent availability of another role is leaked through legal masks: all active commands are attempts.",
    "Raw terminal state is absorbing; the previous terminal causes and clock remain fixed."
  ]
